      "text": "To solve the problem, let's denote the two-digit number \\( n \\) as \\( 10a + b \\), where \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) are the digits of \\( n \\), and \\( a \\) is the tens digit, while \\( b \\) is the units digit. When we switch the digits, the new number becomes \\( 10b + a \\).\n\nAccording to the problem, switching the digits and then adding 3 results in \\( 2n \\). So, we can write the equation:\n\\[\n10b + a + 3 = 2(10a + b)\n\\]\nExpanding and simplifying the right side of the equation, we get:\n\\[\n10b + a + 3 = 20a + 2b\n\\]\nRearranging the terms to isolate \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) on one side, we have:\n\\[\n10b + a + 3 - 2b - 20a = 0\n\\]\n\\[\n8b - 19a + 3 = 0\n\\]\nRearranging further, we get:\n\\[\n8b = 19a - 3\n\\]\nSince \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) are digits (i.e., integers between 0 and 9), \\( 19a - 3 \\) must be divisible by 8. We need to find the smallest positive integer solutions for \\( a \\) and \\( b \\) that satisfy this equation.\n\nLet's test the values of \\( a \\) starting from the smallest possible value, which is 1:\n\\[\n19a - 3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\n\\[\n19a \\equiv 3 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\nSince \\( 19 \\equiv 3 \\pmod{8} \\), we can rewrite the equation as:\n\\[\n3a \\equiv 3 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\nDividing both sides by 3 (which is valid since 3 has an inverse modulo 8, and the inverse of 3 modulo 8 is 3, because \\( 3 \\times 3 = 9 \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8} \\)), we get:\n\\[\na \\equiv 1 \\pmod{8}\n\\]\nThe smallest positive integer \\( a \\) that satisfies this congruence is \\( a = 1 \\). Now, substituting \\( a = 1 \\) back into the equation \\( 8b = 19a - 3 \\), we get:\n\\[\n8b = 19 \\times 1 - 3\n\\]\n\\[\n8b = 16\n\\]\n\\[\nb = 2\n\\]\nSo, the two-digit number \\( n \\) is \\( 10a + b = 10 \\times 1 + 2 = 12 \\).\n\nTo verify, we switch the digits of 12 to get 21, and then add 3:\n\\[\n21 + 3 = 24\n\\]\nAnd \\( 2n \\) is:\n\\[\n2 \\times 12 = 24\n\\]\nSince both sides are equal, the solution is correct. Therefore, the smallest two-digit integer \\( n \\) is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{12}\n\\]",
